## Coverage and mechanism

- T1 embedded corpus, list/check, bounded loops, seed ordering, rate units, refusal, read-only cwd, SIGINT restoration, closed downstream pipe, and real terminal screen semantics all retain tests.
- `paced_with_clock` is private. Its body equals the original pacer after substituting elapsed/pause/stop callbacks; the public caller still supplies Instant, the original 20 ms sleep cap and the same signal flag. Production behavior, flags, error prose and corpus are unchanged.
- Four corpus test bodies and all 14 corpus/provenance/hash files are byte-identical to the base. No manifest, dependency, wire or golden edit.
- Real CLI boundaries remain only where T1 directly names the binary output or OS signal/pipe behavior; parser cases use the existing pure Options seam. No boundary is replaced by a mock.
- Reported test-run time: 0.99 s before, 0.22 s after; 14/0 to 15/0, no ignored tests. These are measurements, never pass predicates. Explicit test sleep calls: 0 before / 0 after; two physical pacing waits and one wall-clock speed assertion removed.
- Crate tests, inventory and strict all-target clippy exited 0; exact command states and raw output are retained for the combined evidence commit. No operator, Keychain, production identity or network fixture.
- No active peer path overlap at the base. One combined land/presubmit covers the four assigned crates; no per-crate full gate.
